{
  "$comment": [
    "Retrieval golden set for the MTC clinical library. Run it with:",
    "  node_modules/.bin/tsx scripts/eval-retrieval.mts",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS: every retrieval knob in this product — embedding model,",
    "output dimensions, chunk size, similarity floor, the trust bonus, the RRF",
    "constant — used to be tunable with no way of telling whether a change helped.",
    "A regression in retrieval raises no error and shows no stack trace: the",
    "hypotheses simply come back with fewer sources and nobody notices.",
    "",
    "EXPECTATIONS ARE BY `metadata.key`, NEVER BY DOCUMENT UUID. Ids differ",
    "between local, staging and production; the key ('ponto:IG4') is stable and",
    "was assigned at import.",
    "",
    "TWO TIERS, and the difference is honesty about who verified them:",
    "  * identifier — a code or pinyin name resolves to exactly one card. This is",
    "    objectively checkable, needs no clinical judgement, and is precisely what",
    "    a 768-dim embedding handles worst. These gate CI.",
    "  * clinical — a practitioner's question paraphrased from what the document",
    "    itself records. Grounded in the corpus (never copied verbatim, which",
    "    would let lexical search win for free and measure nothing), but the",
    "    EXPECTATION still needs a TCM professional to confirm. They are marked",
    "    verified:false and are reported separately until that review happens.",
    "",
    "Adding a case: keep the query in the words a practitioner would actually",
    "type, and make `expect` the smallest set that is genuinely correct."
  ],
